## Approach

This is a backtracking search. The grid is at most 10×10 and there are at most 7 tiles, so the search is small enough.

1. Find the first empty cell in row-major order. Every cell must be covered, so the tile covering this cell must have its top-left corner here. If no empty cell remains, the tiling is complete.
2. For each unused tile, try both orientations (A×B and B×A, deduplicated when A = B). If the rectangle fits inside the grid and all its cells are empty, place it, mark the tile as used, and recurse.
3. If the recursion fails, undo the placement and try the next option.

Because the first empty cell must be covered by some tile placed with its top-left corner there, this search is exhaustive. It covers every tiling that exists.

