def maximumJumps(nums, target):
    n = len(nums)
    NEG = float('-inf')
    dp = [NEG] * n
    dp[0] = 0
    for j in range(1, n):
        for i in range(j):
            if dp[i] != NEG and -target <= nums[j] - nums[i] <= target:
                if dp[i] + 1 > dp[j]:
                    dp[j] = dp[i] + 1
    return dp[n - 1] if dp[n - 1] != NEG else -1
```

**Approach:** `dp[i]` holds the maximum number of jumps needed to reach index `i` from index `0`, or `-inf` if it is unreachable. Index 0 starts at 0 jumps. For each index `j`, we look at every earlier index `i` that is reachable and satisfies the difference constraint, and take the best `dp[i] + 1`. The answer is `dp[n-1]`, or `-1` if it remains unreachable. Time complexity is O(n²) and space is O(n).

